Limit: production composes one daemon per process (agentcpd main creates exactly one), so a live deployment never had two daemons over one control plane; the defect was reachable only where one control plane is given more than one Daemon, as tests such as CP-S59 do
Limit: a control plane whose daemon has been constructed but not started, or has stopped with no successor started, answers every doctor door without the supplemental findings; a caller that takes the lock directly instead of calling start() gets reports without them, which is why the Telegram live-ingress fixture now calls start()
Ruled-out: keep the constructor registration and have the supplier return nothing unless this daemon holds the lock | the refused daemon's registration still replaces the live daemon's supplier, and the empty answer is exactly the defect
Ruled-out: append suppliers instead of replacing | appending doubles every finding the previous supplier still reads, so a report would misstate how many holders are unwakeable
Ruled-out: clear the supplier unconditionally in stop() | a predecessor stopping after its successor registered would leave the successor's doors answering from nothing, so removal is by identity
Warn: stop() now removes this daemon's supplier, so doctor reports on that control plane carry no supplemental findings between one daemon stopping and the next one starting; a refused daemon's stop() removes nothing because it registered nothing
